          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: Two witnesses report an observation made on October 14, 2009, around 9 PM: looking south, the main witness sees in the starry sky a large, gray shape moving silently north. Inside the shape, a sparkling ball is spotted. The second witness confirms the presence of a large white circle that has the consistency of smoke. No other testimony will be collected. The witnesses' descriptions are too imprecise to allow for a hypothesis. The case is classified as C.",
